# Documentation

## Purpose

Keep human docs and AI context/memory matching the real source — never invented.

## When Applied

Editing `docs/**`, `ai/**`, `AGENTS.md`, or `README_AI.md`.

## Requirements

- Document only real, verified conventions (source > SQL > memory > docs precedence).
- Human docs live under [`docs/`](../../../docs/): `architecture/`, `database/`, `product/`, `security/`, `operations/`, `decisions/`, plus `generated/` for machine output only.
- New pages use [`docs/_templates/doc-page.md`](../../../docs/_templates/doc-page.md); new ADRs use [`docs/_templates/adr.md`](../../../docs/_templates/adr.md).
- Update the folder `README.md` index when adding or migrating a page.
- When behavior changes, update the matching [`ai/context/`](../../../ai/context/) pack and, if a decision/lesson, [`ai/memory/`](../../../ai/memory/) or an ADR under [`docs/decisions/`](../../../docs/decisions/).
- Prefer linking to the canonical file over re-explaining it (avoid duplication).
- Respect [`../core/01-change-discipline.mdc`](../core/01-change-discipline.mdc): docs-only tasks don't touch `lib/`.
- `ai/` templates stay empty until filled from real conventions.

## Examples

- New RPC shipped → note it in `ai/context/` and `docs/database/` (or root `supabase-schema-and-rpc.md` until migrated), link from the feature doc.
- New stack constraint → file an ADR under `docs/decisions/` and reference it from `AGENTS.md` if it becomes non-negotiable.

## Anti-patterns

- Inventing conventions to fill a template.
- Copy-pasting content that already lives in another doc.
- Hand-editing `docs/generated/**`.

## Common Mistakes

- Updating code but leaving `ai/memory/` and context packs stale.
- Editing generated docs by hand (see [`generated-files.mdc`](generated-files.mdc)).
- Putting product behaviour in `architecture/` or RLS threat-model prose only in `database/`.
